 Robustness evaluation is limited to experiments where inputs were removed or degraded in a controlled way. Studies with external datasets focus on re-using architectures, fitting to specific datasets, and selected transfer methods, rather than testing if an unchanged model works in a new domain.
 Therefore, the conclusions only apply to the architectures, prediction targets, and evaluation conditions studied. Independent welding validation, predictive audio integration, prospective monitoring, and further operational validation are beyond the completed empirical scope of this work.
